@startuml STM-3
!include _style.iuml
title STM-3 (System level) — Lifecycle of a Charge Point\ncharge_points.lifecycle · v1.1 · 10/11/2026

[*] --> registered
note left of registered
  created when the Admin registers
  the serial number (UC-ADM-03)
end note
registered --> awaiting_connection : Operator onboards it to a site\n/ create connectors, issue credential
awaiting_connection : Charge Point connects [wrong credential]\n/ reject connection, log attempt
awaiting_connection --> in_service : Charge Point connects [credential valid]\n/ read capabilities «planned»,\nshow on map
in_service : Charge Point restarts\n/ read capabilities again «planned»
in_service --> disabled : Operator takes it out of service\n/ hide from search
disabled --> in_service : Operator returns it to service\n/ show in search
disabled --> decommissioned : Admin retires it
decommissioned --> [*]

note right of in_service
  Online / offline is not a lifecycle state:
  it is kept as a connection flag
  (is_online, last_seen_at). An in_service
  Charge Point can be offline; a disabled
  one can be online. Offline alert: STM-6.
end note
@enduml
